  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On a chase from a sinkhole, Wu Ji of Wu clan demands that Kong Ri Tian leave behind the Gu worms of Sheng Tian true inheritance, and other Southern Border Gu Masters treat that prize as a Gu Immortal true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        2095
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_empress_wu_ji",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "char_kong_ri_tian",
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Zhen Zhu says Wu Ji already obtained Sheng Tian true inheritance from Kong Sheng Tian, yet still pursued Kong Ri Tian instead of handing the prize to the clan. Wu Zhan Ping later names that same retrieval as Wu clan’s third high-value true inheritance on offer, left by Kong Sheng Tian, a famous qi path Gu Immortal most skilled at movement methods. Kong Sheng Tian held qi escape Immortal Gu, once fourth on the List of Mystical Gu before Spring Autumn Cicada’s rise pushed it down, and he created a qi path movement killer move also named Kong Sheng Tian. Wu Zhan Ping adds that the Immortal Gu from the true inheritance are likely already with Kong Ri Tian.",
      "chapters": [
        2096
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "creator-and-retrieval",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_zhen_zhu",
        "char_kong_sheng_tian",
        "char_wu_zhan_ping",
        "sys_immortal_gu",
        "sys_ten_big_mystical_gu",
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At first only rank five experts such as Wu Ji and Shang Xin Ci press Kong Ri Tian, but once Sheng Tian true inheritance is exposed, Southern Border’s super clans send Gu Immortals after it. Kong Ri Tian and his group eventually hide at Rotten Mud Mountain, where a Wu clan Gu Immortal corners them. Kong Sheng Tian’s will rides with Kong Ri Tian, and beyond the will in the true inheritance there are also Immortal Gu and immortal essence that let Kong Ri Tian use Gu Immortal methods while fleeing.",
      "chapters": [
        2098
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "immortal-pursuit",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shang_xin_ci",
        "loc_rotten_mud_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Yong later notes that other forces know about Sheng Tian true inheritance but not about Hu Land, and he classes Sheng Tian true inheritance as a rank eight inheritance that would once have shaken all of Southern Border’s Gu Immortal world.",
      "chapters": [
        2099
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "inheritance-rank",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_yong",
        "loc_hu_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Yong agrees to let Fang Yuan have Sheng Tian true inheritance, judging that giving it up helps Wu clan keep Hu Land secret. Wu clan has only just obtained the true inheritance, and Wu Yong states that it has contents but not Immortal Gu, because the Immortal Gu and immortal essence remain with Kong Ri Tian. Through Ke Xin Hong and treasure yellow heaven, Fang Yuan pays a rank nine wind path immortal material and receives the full details of Sheng Tian true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        2101
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trade-handover",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_ke_xin_hong"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ke Xin Hong tells Wu Yong that Wu clan excels in wind path and that its only qi path foundation is in Sheng Tian true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        2134
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "qi-path-foundation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
